  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nWhat changed: `a_trickling_client_is_dropped_on_the_idle_schedule` (crates/app/tests/mcp_live.rs) now accepts a connection reset, abort, broken pipe or EOF after the idle deadline as the drop. The server was read and is correct: on the idle deadline it writes a best-effort note and closes a socket that still holds the trickler's unread bytes, and TCP answers that close with an RST that can overtake the note under load. A read timeout (client still connected) or a note without \"idle\" still fails, and the existing timing bounds (>=350 ms, <1500 ms) and the server log assertion are kept. No retries, no longer sleeps. The sibling idle test (no trickled bytes, so no unread data at close) was checked and does not have this race.\n\nTested: whole mcp_live binary 20/20 with --test-threads=16 under 8 busy-loop CPU hogs; the single test 20/20; `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green; clippy -D warnings on camcraft-app clean. Not exercised: macOS.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1366\n",
